{"title":"Kinetic energy","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Kinetic_Energy\">Kinetic Energy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kinetic_energy&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Kinetic Energy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Simply put, kinetic energy is the amount of movement energy an object possesses. It is given by the formula K=1/2*mass*velocity^2. Notable theorems include the work energy theorem W=change in kinetic energy and the Conservation of energy theorem, Ki+Ui=Kf+Uf.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>See <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Potential_Energy&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Potential Energy (page does not exist)\">Potential Energy</a>.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Kinetic_energy&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170726\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 8/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.461      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.461      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27487:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017170726 and revision id 271752. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}